From: Deyan Petrov <25847560+deyanp@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 30 Aug 2026 21:09:53 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 6/6] local: remap command bytes to the Raffstore/venetian
 variant
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

NOT UPSTREAMABLE. This is a per-installation choice.

The 7 Schlotterer-badged Elero Raffstore blinds in this house use Elero's
extended command byte set, where a short press steps the slats and a long
press starts a full travel:

  0x10 stop          0x20 tilt step open    0x21 full travel up
  0x24 ventilation   0x40 tilt step closed  0x41 full down, no tilt
  0x44 full down + restore tilt

Upstream's UP (0x20) and DOWN (0x40) are the short-press bytes here, so with
upstream defaults Home Assistant can only nudge the slats — the blind never
travels. Remap:

  UP            0x20 -> 0x21
  DOWN          0x40 -> 0x44
  TILT_UP            =  0x20  (no longer an alias of UP)
  TILT_DOWN          =  0x40  (no longer an alias of DOWN)
  TILT          0x24 -> VENTILATION 0x24
  INTERMEDIATE  0x44 -> DOWN_NO_TILT 0x41

Follow-on renames in elero_strings.cpp and cover_sm.cpp, which can no longer
rely on TILT_UP == UP. Unit tests updated for the new names; the golden vector
layout test now compares against command::UP rather than the literal 0x20,
because it checks the packet layout and not the byte value.

Changing these globals would break every other user's motors, so upstream
needs per-device configurable command bytes instead:
https://github.com/manuschillerdev/esphome-elero/issues/63

Sources: Elero transmitter-stick documentation;
https://github.com/andyboeh/esphome-elero/issues/4

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
